    "prompt": "The StratifiedKFold documentation is misleading. Currently, the documentation for the shuffle parameter states that it shuffles each stratification of the data before splitting into batches, but in reality, the implementation shuffles the order of batches instead of shuffling the actual samples within each class. This discrepancy causes confusion because even when shuffle is enabled and different random_state values are used, the batches do not change as expected. The documentation needs to be updated to clearly indicate that, when enabled, shuffle will randomize each class's samples before splitting into batches, ensuring that different random_state values produce different shuffles.",
    "hint_texts": "Focus on updating the docstring for the shuffle parameter in the StratifiedKFold class. Change the description from 'shuffle each stratification of the data before splitting into batches' to 'shuffle each class's samples before splitting into batches'. Ensure that the updated text accurately reflects the intended behavior and is consistent with the overall documentation style.",
    "entrypoint": "File: sklearn/model_selection/_split.py; update the docstring in the StratifiedKFold class, particularly in the section describing the 'shuffle' parameter in its __init__ method.",
    "tests": {
      "FAIL_TO_PASS": "No test cases are applicable for a documentation update.",
      "PASS_TO_PASS": "Documentation review should confirm that the updated text clearly describes that each class's samples are shuffled before splitting into batches."
    }
  },
